# Audited: tap (tick 1) fires the inner's go as tick 2's input, which fires the leaf's hit as tick 3's input, both ticks owed; the leaf's text input, forwarded by the inner host at 1/[1]/0 and by the outer at 1/[1/[1]/0]/0, hears a key in its own tick.
# The nested hosts' tests: declarations of be-host-nested.prism (Semantics chapter 9).

test two_computing_layers_cost_two_ticks, @outer:
    build
    click at 0
        => expect Ui.Label(text="0 hits, 0 keys")
    compute until idle
        => expect Ui.Label(text="1 hits, 0 keys")
    send at 1/[1/[1]/0]/0, Letter "x"
        => expect Ui.Label(text="1 hits, 1 keys")
